From: Tenda AC8 OpenWrt port
Subject: rtl8192cd-rtl8197f: cfg80211/nl80211 for the Tenda AC8 variant

Build the AC8 variant with the Realtek cfg80211 layer (RTK_NL80211)
instead of the legacy wireless extensions, against the cfg80211 of the
mac80211 backports (API of Linux 6.12), so that netifd, hostapd, iw,
iwinfo and LuCI can drive the radios:

- compile with the backports include path and autoconf, depend on
  kmod-cfg80211; the other variants stay on WEXT;
- MadWifi net80211 headers the Realtek OpenWrt SDK ships with the driver
  (dual BSD/GPL), plus the Realtek-only AES-CMAC cipher id;
- cfg80211 API updates behind RTK_CFG80211_API_612: link_id arguments of
  the key/AP/channel ops, cfg80211_ap_update for change_beacon,
  update_mgmt_frame_registrations, no set_wds_peer, per-link CAC state,
  cfg80211_scan_info, nl80211_band names, channel switch notifications
  with link_id and the wiphy mutex, zeroed chandefs, class_create()
  without owner;
- regulatory: queue the domain from the reg notifier
  (regulatory_set_wiphy_regd), set it synchronously after wiphy_register
  under RTNL and the wiphy mutex;
- keep incompatible-pointer, implicit-declaration and int-conversion
  warnings fatal for 8192cd_cfg80211.c;
- install /etc/init.d/rtl8197f-wlan (overlay) with the AC8 variant;
- rtl8197f-wlan-load: ubox modprobe drops module parameters, so load the
  dependencies with modprobe and the driver with insmod.
